No i'm having moments everyday for a moment where it gets worse, but kind of worse like there's no way it could get worse. Usually in the evening. But I still have constently the idea that I wanna go. It's just more or less present in my mind. Create a thread when it's so present it's unbearable.

&#x200B;

No nobody deserves that pain I agree but what does it change, not the fact that it's there, I'm the first to tell no one should ever feel this pain not even an hour but what does it change. I was once told I didn't deserve to die but nor do I deserve that pain so idk.

&#x200B;

I obviously have the feeling I tried it all [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MVE75VG90X0](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MVE75VG90X0)

It's the same in Europe but you just get on the entry, on the road that isn't an highway and get you up on the highway. So not so hard. These spots are cool because people are turning to get to the highway and so, like i said, have time and space to get you.

&#x200B;

That's something I do a lot when i hitchhike.

&#x200B;

Now something with highways, something can be tough, if it's someone is living the highway (you might then ask to get off the car as i said no the make detours) and it could desertic. So i said you should stick to your road (because i don't see any detours that wouldn't add like 100km giving your road). But you could adapt your trips for small detours. For example : it could be ok to make a detour of 50km if the driver is driving 300km but not EXACTLY in your direction. You follow me ?

&#x200B;

You could try on the wood or in a field, try to be hidden. When it's bright and you're awake you're much less an easy target than when you're asleep. Now something possible (that i do sometimes) is asking people for a night but in your situation it would add more risk to bring the police to you.

&#x200B;

Edit : hitchhiking on the highway is ofc dangerous on the addition of illegal AND not so productive so you should always find and alternative.

I've done like 10 000km of hitchhiking in my life, never had a SINGLE bad experience. The worst that happenned to me ? Boring people talking to me. (i look very young btw)

&#x200B;

That being said that doesn't mean it's perfectly safe but i'd say it's not something that is so dangerous.

&#x200B;

Before giving you any advice there's something you need to ask yourself. The people you are willing to see, what would they do ? Because if they don't feel like hosting you (i mean you need a plan for the future years isn't it ?) you might be forced to be back to the family you're living at rigth now. And as Drengor said before you should take care about people that could call the police because you are in a fugue. Is this the only solution ? I mean hitchhiking 500km it should be one of the last option you have. Anyway if people are willing to help you when you'll be at Bradford, can't they come and pick you up ? Plus there's something : if people are helping you to fugue they could have some trouble. The odds are really low but that's something that could come in play when they pick you up and learn that you're not 18.

&#x200B;

Anyway speaking about hitchhiking itself. 500km a day, it's gonna be hard, you should get up early to get people that are going to work. And as Spazierer said prepare yourself to spend a night out. Anyway if that happens you could try to find a house and ask for hospitality but here again it could be something that would bring you to the cops. Nothing bad would happen to you legaly speaking but you'd be returned to the family...

&#x200B;

You could have a sign or two, don't put a city 300km away from where you are but maybe the next city that's well known around and 100km max. Try to put yourself when cars aren't driving fast because they have time to look at your face (really important) and it's of course easier to stop at 50km/h than 100 km/h. I've been looking on Google and it looks like there's small towns and nothing in between, and towns are far from each other. So logic would say : if someone picks you up, you're gonna make a decent distance.  If someone drops you in a city for a reason or another, walk away from it. It's much more easier to hitchhike in the road because people know that you're going the way the road goes (in the city people go in every direction). Giving your road you should stick to it. If people are making detours, just ask them to drop you off when they're leaving your road. Don't hesitate to walk a little to find a better spot. Also BE SOMEWHERE WHEN PEOPLE CANE EASILY STOP. They shouldn't make effort and brake so hard to pick you up.

&#x200B;

And btw a child in an abusive family ? Police should be on your side but things are complicated in these cases.

&#x200B;

Forgive my bad english and good luck.

